1950’s restoration. The condition shows the typical restoration of the cars that were sold throughout the ’40s and ’50’s – often the owner had a working restoration done on their “baby” or they bought already used cars for the money they could get for them then restored and resold them to the people who wanted the cars for the cars themselves.
The engine has been modified, rebuilt and tuned by Larry Taylor, and drives beautifully. The transmission has also been rebuilt and retuned by Taylor.
All of the mechanical work has an expert eye on it… the body was straightened front to rear; all the front leaf springs have replaced the damaged front end; the rear axle rebuilt; the front wheel bearings rebuilt; and the steering head fixed to return the movement to normal operation; the front tires and all four shocks are new – all but one tire has brand name tires – the last one will be replaced; the radiator cap has a newer one installed; front headlights and driver’s side fog indicator are all new;

